# ROMs and user assets must never be committed to this repository.
*.nes
*.unf
*.fds
*.3dn

# A pattern without a slash is matched against every path component, directories
# included -- and case-insensitively on Windows. "*.nes" therefore also matches the
# directories "src/Zax.Nes" and "src/Zax.Nes/..."; without these negations the whole NES
# core would be silently left out of the repository. The negations re-include the source
# trees only: no .nes file inside them is ever un-ignored, and tests/roms has its own
# .gitignore.
!src/Zax.Nes/

# Dear ImGui layout dump (persistence is off; this only appears if it is re-enabled)
imgui.ini

# User data. REQ-PERS-071: a "portable.txt" next to the executable moves the settings, the
# save states, the battery RAM, the covers and the imported .3dn profiles into "userdata/"
# beside it -- which, run from a build output inside the tree, lands in the repository.
userdata/
portable.txt

# Assets the user supplies for the optional "--assets <dir>" mode, when they are copied into a
# build output: never published from here, never committed.
# Anchored to the root on purpose -- a bare "assets/" would also match "src/Zax.Render/Assets/",
# since Windows matches these patterns without regard to case.
/assets-neutral/
/assets/
